          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "গরিব (gôrib) is a loan from Arabic gharīb, \"a stranger\", which reached Bengali through Persian. Its Arabic root is gh-r-b (Lane). In Bengali, as in Hindi, it has come to mean \"poor\"."
            }
          ]
        },
